[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Danish Gambit"]
[Variation "Danish Gambit Accepted: Classical Defense"]
[ECO "C21"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap"]
[Themes "development-lead,long-diagonal,gambit-compensation"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "3...dxc3 4.Bc4 cxb2 5.Bxb2 Nf6"]
[Start "danish-gambit-declined 3.c3"]

3... dxc3 4. Bc4 { Offers a second pawn. In return the bishop aims at f7 and White gets fast development along open lines toward Black's king. } 4... cxb2 5. Bxb2 { Wins one pawn back and aims the bishop down the long diagonal at g7 and the rook on h8. Two pawns down, White now plays for speed. } 5... Nf6 ( 5... Bb4+ 6. Nc3 Nf6 7. Qb3 ) 6. Nc3 { Brings out a piece and defends e4, so the knight on f6 cannot take that pawn for free. White needs every piece in play quickly. } 6... Bb4 ( 6... d5 7. Nxd5 { Takes the pawn back before Black's centre grows. } 7... Nxd5 8. exd5 { Takes back with the pawn, which opens the e-file and keeps both bishops. } 8... Bb4+ 9. Kf1 { The king has to move, so White loses the right to castle. White is a little worse but keeps the bishops and open lines. } ) ( 6... Nc6 7. Nf3 { Develops and prepares to castle. } 7... Bb4 8. O-O Bxc3 9. Bxc3 ) 7. Qb3 { Attacks the bishop on b4 and, with the bishop on c4, doubles up on f7. Black must trade or lose time. } 7... Bxc3+ 8. Qxc3 { The queen and the bishop on b2 now line up on the long diagonal toward g7. Black has to watch the kingside while still behind in development. } 8... d6 9. Nf3 { Develops and clears the way to castle. Next White wants e4-e5 to open the long diagonal for the queen and bishop. } 9... O-O 10. O-O { Gets the king safe now that the centre is open. } 10... Nc6 11. Rfe1 { Supports a coming e4-e5. Plan: push e5 to open the diagonal toward g7, keep the pieces active and do not trade them off while a pawn down. White ends a little worse, which is the price of the gambit. } 11... Bg4 *
